<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>The smoothing trick</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a smoothing variance
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, write</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}\coloneqq\pi*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)\,,\qquad\Pi_{\eta}\coloneqq\pi_{\eta}\otimes\mathsf{N}(0,I)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}\coloneqq\pi*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)\,,\qquad\Pi_{\eta}\coloneqq\pi_{\eta}\otimes\mathsf{N}(0,I)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S3.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">key algorithmic idea</span> of this paper is to pick a smoothing parameter
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and to sample from the smoothed distribution <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>
instead of the original target <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. If
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\law(Y)\approx\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\law(Y)\approx\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we can recover a sample from <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> via
the RGO: for <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim R_{\eta,Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim R_{\eta,Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\law(X)\approx\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\law(X)\approx\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The smoothed
potential <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined by
<math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-V_{\eta}}\coloneqq e^{-V}*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-V_{\eta}}\coloneqq e^{-V}*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)</annotation></semantics></math>, is given by</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V_{\eta}(y)=\mathbb{E}\bigl[\nabla V(X)\bigm|X+\sqrt{\eta}\,G=y\bigr]\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V_{\eta}(y)=\mathbb{E}\bigl[\nabla V(X)\bigm|X+\sqrt{\eta}\,G=y\bigr]\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\pi</annotation></semantics></math> are independent.
The smoothed potential admits quantitative higher-order derivative bounds, allowing us to apply higher-order integrators.
The catch is that (<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 3.1 ‣ 3.1 The smoothing trick ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>) is given as a conditional expectation, and is therefore not explicitly computable.
Write <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\eta}\coloneqq\nabla V_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}\coloneqq\nabla V_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we replace evaluations of <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> with</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)\coloneqq\nabla V\bigl(\operatorname{prox}_{\eta V}(y)+\sqrt{\eta}\,G\bigr)\,,\qquad G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)\coloneqq\nabla V\bigl(\operatorname{prox}_{\eta V}(y)+\sqrt{\eta}\,G\bigr)\,,\qquad G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The intuition is that
<math id="S3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla V_{\eta}(y)=\int\nabla V\,\mathrm{d}R_{\eta,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo>∫</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V_{\eta}(y)=\int\nabla V\,\mathrm{d}R_{\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="S3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\law(\operatorname{prox}_{\eta V}(y)+\sqrt{\eta}\,G)\approx R_{\eta,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\law(\operatorname{prox}_{\eta V}(y)+\sqrt{\eta}\,G)\approx R_{\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that
<math id="S3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)</annotation></semantics></math> is almost an unbiased estimator of
<math id="S3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V_{\eta}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V_{\eta}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>